f 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\cos^2 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723266}] [{:answer/feedback "The derivative of $\\cos t$ supplies another factor of $\\sin t$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\sin^5 t\\cos^4 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723267}] [{:answer/feedback "This comes from $y(t)x^{\\prime}(t)$. The given $P=0$, $Q=x$ requires $-x(t)y^{\\prime}(t)$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\cos^6 t\\sin^4 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723269}] [{:answer/feedback "The boundary is positively oriented, so there is no extra minus sign." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6\\cos^2 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723271}] [{:answer/feedback "Include the factor $2$ from $y^{\\prime}(t)$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\cos^2 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723272}] [{:answer/feedback "Use the supplied $y^{\\prime}(t)=2\\cos t$, not $y(t)=2\\sin t$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\sin^2 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723275}] [{:answer/feedback "The power rule supplies a factor of $5$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin^6 t\\cos^4 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723276}] [{:answer/feedback "Multiply $x(t)$ by $y^{\\prime}(t)$, not by $y(t)$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6\\sin t\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723277}] [{:answer/feedback "The differential is $\\mathrm dx$, so differentiate $e^{\\cos t}$, not $e^{\\sin t}$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sin t\\,e^{2\\sin t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723278}] [{:answer/feedback "Correct: $-(\\sin^5 t)(-5\\cos^4 t\\sin t)=5\\sin^6 t\\cos^4 t$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\sin^6 t\\cos^4 t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186723279}] [{:answer/feedback "The minus in $P=-y$ cancels the minus in $x^{\\prime}(t)$." :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-